  "problem": "The rate at which customers enter a store one afternoon is given by the function\n\n$$\nr(t)=6{e}^{t}+3,\n$$\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in customers per hour and $t>0$ is the time in hours since $1\\,\\text{p.m}.$\nCustomers are also leaving the store at a steady rate of $5$ customers per hour.\n\nIf there were $40$ customers in the store at $1\\,\\text{p.m},$ how many customers will be there at $4\\,\\text{p.m}?$\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, there will be \n{{field-1}}  customers in the store at $4\\,\\text{p.m}.$",
